---
/** "Read with care" for the shortage area pages: what a count counts, what a mark is, and what the tracker does not say. */
import { COUNT_COLUMNS, day, getIndex } from '../../lib/hc-areas';

interface Props {
  /** True on a state's page, which has lists of designations and sites. */
  state?: boolean;
}
const { state = false } = Astro.props;
const when = day(getIndex().snapshot_day);
---

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="read-with-care">
  <div class="note">
    <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="8.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"></circle><path d="M10 9v5M10 6v.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg>
    <div>
      <p><strong id="read-with-care">Read with care.</strong> Every figure, status, score and date is HRSA’s, from its files of {when}, and is printed as HRSA published it. ClinX has not changed, rounded, added up or estimated a value. The counts are counts of rows in those files.</p>
      <p>{COUNT_COLUMNS}</p>
      <p>A designation belongs to the state HRSA gives as its primary state. Its counties can lie in other states, and its row names them. A cell HRSA leaves empty is shown as Blank in HRSA’s file. Where HRSA writes NA or Not Applicable in a cell, the page prints it as HRSA wrote it. They are HRSA’s own marks for a value that does not apply or is not given.</p>
      {
        state && (
          <p>Proposed For Withdrawal is a status HRSA gives a designation in its file. The page states the status and says nothing about what follows from it. The files do not say why a designation was designated, withdrawn or updated, and the page does not say why either. A date in the last 365 days is when HRSA says the event happened. The day of the copy is when ClinX saw it, so HRSA may have entered a change earlier than the day a copy shows it.</p>
        )
      }
      <p>No state is ranked or compared with another here. States and territories are listed A to Z. HRSA’s files still hold withdrawn designations from many years ago, so a count of Withdrawn is a count of rows HRSA still publishes. <a href="/methods/">Methods</a> describes how ClinX copies and checks public files.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
